00:24:59.000 --> 00:25:39.000
making more money. I'm just wondering, does having more money make people happier? That's a question that moral philosophers and poets and artists and people have thought about, not just about money, but about resources for as long as we've had them. So these are long-standing questions. And there are questions that we have some answers to, but I think the work is ongoing. There's new work that suggests that maybe, in fact, the plateau isn't at $70,000, but it's much later. And as your money goes up, happiness does, but the incremental value of each sort of rise in income starts to diminish.

39
