wealth seeps into the mind. And you pointed at this other really interesting piece, this emotional experience of guilt. And so we've been in the lab now for the last six or seven years, been looking at the role of guilt, particularly in a climate of growing inequality. The role of guilt in how people experience their wealth and how that guilt, those feelings of undeservingness, play into not only how someone feels about their wealth, but also what they're willing to do with it. So we've gotten interested in this idea of wealth guilt and where it comes from. And what are the ways that people go, what are the lengths that people go to assuage those feelings of guilt, to mitigate them and to even try to alleviate them, not only within themselves,

